==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*haitaną|t=command, name}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*kei-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ki-|t=put in motion, be moving}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|hēta}}, {{cog|osx|hētan}}, {{cog|goh|heizzan}}, {{cog|non|heita}} ({{cog|sv|heta}}), {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|grc|κίειν|t=put in motion}}, {{cog|la|ciere|t=rouse, make active}} and {{cog|sq|cys|t=to spur, set in motion}}.

===Pronunciation===
